      en: "Tembiaporá, in the Caaguazú department, is recognized as the 'Banana Capital' of Paraguay. This region's humid, subtropical climate is perfect for the production of high-quality bananas, which are a major staple of the national diet and an increasingly important export. The vast plantations of the Tembiaporá district are managed primarily by small and medium-sized farmers who have organized into cooperatives to improve their marketing and logistical capacity. Paraguayan bananas are now exported in large quantities to the Argentine and Uruguayan markets. The sector is a vital source of income and pride for the local community, showcasing the potential of specialty fruit production. Geography K7 — fruit production and regional specialties."
